From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AMI OpenBMC <support@ami.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] netfilter: nf_tables: add missing break in
 nf_tables_deactivate_set()

The NFT_TRANS_PREPARE_ERROR case in nf_tables_deactivate_set() is missing
the terminating "break;" statement, so control falls through into the
NFT_TRANS_PREPARE case. Besides being a logic error (set->use would be
decremented twice for the PREPARE_ERROR phase), this triggers:

  net/netfilter/nf_tables_api.c: In function 'nf_tables_deactivate_set':
  net/netfilter/nf_tables_api.c:5976:17: error: this statement may fall
  through [-Werror=implicit-fallthrough=]

On machines that build the kernel with CONFIG_WERROR=y (e.g. intel-ast2600)
this warning is promoted to an error and breaks do_compile, while machines
without CONFIG_WERROR only emit a warning.

Restore the upstream behaviour by terminating the PREPARE_ERROR case with
a break, matching mainline Linux.

Upstream-Status: Backport

Signed-off-by: AMI OpenBMC <support@ami.com>
---
 net/netfilter/nf_tables_api.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/net/netfilter/nf_tables_api.c b/net/netfilter/nf_tables_api.c
index 0000000000000..1111111111111 100644
--- a/net/netfilter/nf_tables_api.c
+++ b/net/netfilter/nf_tables_api.c
@@ -5973,6 +5973,7 @@ void nf_tables_deactivate_set(const struct nft_ctx *ctx, struct nft_set *set,
 			list_del_rcu(&binding->list);
 
 		nft_use_dec(&set->use);
+		break;
 	case NFT_TRANS_PREPARE:
 		if (nft_set_is_anonymous(set)) {
 			if (set->flags & (NFT_SET_MAP | NFT_SET_OBJECT))
-- 
